//! The `page-break-after` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property adjusts
//! page breaks _after_ the current element.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | always | avoid | left | right | inherit
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#propdef-page-break-after
//!
//! Author guide:
